        "\n",
        "## USD/TWD Exchange Rate Forecast Model\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.card}\n",
        "A medium-horizon forecasting framework for USD/TWD combining macro fundamentals and market microstructure signals.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "### Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "- Forecast 1-week to 1-month USD/TWD direction and volatility.\n",
        "- Provide explainable factor attribution for each forecast.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Data Inputs\n",
        "\n",
        "- Taiwan and US rate differentials.\n",
        "- DXY, risk sentiment, and regional FX basket.\n",
        "- Taiwan export orders, PMI surprises, and foreign equity flow.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Modeling Stack\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Baseline: regularized linear model (Elastic Net).\n",
        "2. Nonlinear layer: gradient boosting for interaction terms.\n",
        "3. Regime switch: hidden Markov model for low/high-volatility states.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Signal Equation\n",
        "\n",
        "A stylized prediction equation:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\hat{\\Delta s}_{t+1} = \\alpha + \\sum_{k=1}^{K} w_k x_{k,t} + g(x_t)\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $x_{k,t}$ is macro/market feature $k$ and $g(\\cdot)$ captures nonlinear interactions.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Minimal Python Prototype"
      ],
      "id": "c66dddf8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from sklearn.linear_model import ElasticNet\n",
        "\n",
        "# df should contain columns: y (next-period FX return), and feature columns\n",
        "features = [\"us_tw_rate_diff\", \"dxy_ret\", \"foreign_flow\", \"risk_sentiment\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "def fit_baseline(df: pd.DataFrame):\n",
        "    model = ElasticNet(alpha=0.01, l1_ratio=0.5, random_state=42)\n",
        "    model.fit(df[features], df[\"y\"])\n",
        "    return model"
      ],
